  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate-responsive agricultural value chains for resilient livelihoods in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to accelerate climate-resilient recovery through locally led regenerative agroforestry by empowering communities, especially women and youth, to design, implement, and scale adaptation actions in the drylands of northern Ethiopia. The project contributes to Ethiopia#s NAP and aims to increase adaptive capacity, reduce climate risks, strengthen sustainable natural resources management, diversify climate-resilient livelihoods, and enhance incomes and employment opportunities. The project will have four components, including: Component 1. Local institutions, climate services &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; finance; Component 2. Regenerative agroforestry &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; diversified livelihoods; Component 3. Value chains, dignified green Jobs, and Component 4. Coordination, Monitoring, and Knowledge Management.</narrative>
  </description>
